  "term": "evoked potential",
  "definition": "An evoked potential is an electrical signal measured from a nerve, muscle, sensory receptor, or part of the central nervous system after stimulation. Different forms are identified by the kind of system stimulated, such as auditory, visual, somatosensory, or motor.",
